1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,320
Think about this: Which file is ready to
be advertised as a guaranteed

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,760
recovery? Let’s work through it together.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:12,380
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 15: Choose a
responsible next action.

4
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:16,680
A case can look attractive while missing
the facts needed for responsible

5
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:22,020
work. Review five areas before
progressing: permitted activity, client

6
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:26,560
authority, reliable evidence, current
funds status, and the need for

7
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:31,560
professional representation. An unknown in
one area must remain visible even

8
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:33,180
when the other areas look complete.

9
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:35,780
Use plain next-action labels.

10
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:40,500
“Organize authorized documents” fits a
file ready for administrative work.

11
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,700
“Await custodian confirmation” fits an
unverified balance.

12
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:49,620
“Refer authority or entitlement issue”
fits a disputed or complex claim.

13
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:54,460
These labels describe tasks; they are not
legal approvals or automatic

14
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:58,800
business scores. A small amount is not a
reason to skip authority checks,

15
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,380
and a large apparent amount is not a
reason to ignore restrictions.

16
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,120
Record why you paused and what evidence
would allow the next permitted step.

17
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:11,180
Protect the client’s interests rather than
chasing a numerical target.

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,240
Pause and try this.

19
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:17,860
Evaluate the fictional capstone file with
one missing authority document and

20
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:19,260
a pending competing claim.

21
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,980
Choose two specific next actions.

22
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:27,000
Quick knowledge check. Which file is ready
to be advertised as a guaranteed

23
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,160
recovery? The answer: None of these
establishes a guaranteed recovery.

24
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:36,400
Administrative readiness, legal
entitlement, and eventual payment are

25
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:40,780
different questions. Keep the source, the
date, and the unknowns visible.

26
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,440
I'll see you in the next lesson.
